{{#if_pure {{equal::{{getvar::scenario_mode}}::1}} }}
Forcing my heavy eyelids open, the first thing I saw was an unfamiliar ceiling. It wasn't the harsh glare of fluorescent lights or the plain wallpaper I was used to. Instead, I was greeted by a high ceiling adorned with intricate, antique molding, and dazzling morning sunlight pouring through the gaps in the window.

I gathered my dazed senses and sat up. The texture of the bedding against my back was unbelievably soft and plush. Looking around, I realized the room was filled with luxurious furniture—the kind you’d only see on a movie set or in a museum. Struggling to make sense of the situation and organize my chaotic thoughts, I climbed out of bed and staggered toward a massive full-length mirror standing in the corner.

<img src="rosetta_default">

The moment I stood before the mirror, my breath hitched. Reflected there was not the self I knew, but a complete stranger.

Gorgeous pink hair cascading down to her waist in waves, ruby eyes as red as blood yet sparkling like jewels, and skin so pale and white it looked devoid of warmth. That sharp, haughty, yet somehow fragile beauty unmistakably belonged to a character from a novel I had read.

The tragic villainess from The Conditions of a Beloved Marquis’s Daughter. A character who desperately struggled to prove her worth, tormented the heroine, 'Alicia,' out of jealousy, and ultimately met a miserable end.

'Rosetta Viola Cardion.'

Watching the woman in the mirror open her mouth and widen her eyes in perfect sync with my movements, I felt a chill run down my spine. An unbelievable reality was staring right back at me from beyond the glass.
